        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0346" n="1080" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1080"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Breckinridge to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                        1895</hi></date>. (Received Oct. 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the legation’s No. 132, of
                    August 24, I now have to inclose translation of a note just received from Mr.
                    Chichkine stating that the minister of the interior consents to our missionaries
                    in China entering Siberia without previous condition or agreement, it only being
                    required of them to agree with the local officials in writing to abstain from
                    all interference with religious matters while there.</p>
                <p>I also inclose copy of my note of this date, acknowledging this compliance with
                    the request.</p>
                <p>Mr. Adee’s No. 110, of the 4th instant, expressing gratification at the receipt
                    of my telegram of August 23, is to hand.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clifton R. Breckinridge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



